Command-line companions to Window Maker, grouped by what they act on.


config/ - reading and modifying Window Maker's configuration
=============================================================

wdwrite       write data into the defaults database (configuration files)

wdread        read simple data from the defaults database (for use in
              scripts, for example)

getstyle      get the current style settings and save them into a file, or
              create a theme pack

setstyle      load style settings from a style file and set up Window Maker

convertfonts  rewrite the font specifications in a style file to the
              fontconfig syntax

geticonset    output the current set of icon assignments; good for making
              themes

seticons      merge icon definitions into the WMWindowAttributes file


menu/ - generating root menus
==============================

wmgenmenu     generate a menu from the applications found on the system

wmmenugen     generate a menu from XDG .desktop files or wm-config data


desktop/ - command-line clients acting on a running X session
==============================================================

(The graphical programs that used to live here, wmagnify and wmiv, are
applications and now live in src/apps/.)

wmsetbg       set the workspace background to an image and make it persist
              between sessions

wxcopy        copy an input file or stdin into the X cut buffer

wxpaste       copy the content of the X cut buffer to stdout


scripts/ - shell and Perl helpers
==================================

Installed alongside the compiled tools:

wmaker.inst      quick and dirty script to install the necessary files from
                 the global configuration into a user's directory; the
                 build patches the configured paths into it

wm-oldmenu2new   convert between the plain text menu format and the property
                 list menu format

wkdemenu.pl      convert a KDE menu into a Window Maker menu (for pipe)

Run from the source tree, not installed:

bughint          gather system information for a bug report

checkpatch.pl    coding-style checker for patches; see
                 docs/development/submitting-patches.txt

update-changelog.pl  regenerate docs/development/ChangeLog from git history


po/ - translations for the messages these tools print
